From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:54:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 087/127] render: puppet IK chains reach for their animated
 targets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A puppet bone whose simulation JSON (MDLS, parsed by GH 0x14028bbd0) has `ik` (settings flag
0x4000) ends an IK chain `ikd` bones long (≥ 1, settings +0x5c); `ikr` (flag 0x40) turns it to
its target's rotation. MDLS v2's u16 list of IK targets (a name, the bone, a type, a 64-byte
matrix in the mesh's space) is read: type 0 is the chain end's goal, type 1 the pole. MDLA v2's
per-target tracks (keys as the bones') are read and mixed with the animation layers like the
bones. 3042492564's arm (海果-手臂, ikd 2) has static bone tracks and a hand target moving 24 px:
its arm now follows the target instead of staying in the bind pose.

Inferred: WE's solver itself wasn't found in the mixer (GH 0x140228470 holds the Euler limits
and the physics); two-bone chains use the law of cosines with the elbow on the pole's side,
longer ones CCD, in the puppet's plane. ikce / ikrmin / ikrmax (constraints) are not applied.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "F2 result" (F3's leftover IK, 3042492564)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
